# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, regardless of contributor OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout can rewrite whole files to CRLF and produce diffs
# with equal insertion and deletion counts and zero actual content change — which is
# exactly what happened on 2026-11-23 and cost an hour of "what changed?".
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, stores LF, and checks out LF
# everywhere. Modern editors on Windows handle LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and lock files: stored LF, never diffed by eye.
pnpm-lock.yaml  -diff linguist-generated
*.md            text eol=lf diff=markdown

# Binary, never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
